TITLE:: SCVMeter
summary:: Compact, vertical real-time server level meter
categories:: GUI>Visuals
related:: Classes/SCVisuals, Classes/SCVMeterView, Classes/ServerMeter

DESCRIPTION::
SCVMeter provides a compact, modernized vertical level meter for SuperCollider audio servers. It preserves the classic separated Input and Output channel strip arrangement while incorporating:

list::
## High-legibility dB tick ruler (0, -3, -6, -12, -18, -24, -36, -48, -60, -80 dBFS)
## Dynamic palette theming (Graphite, Phosphor, Ice, Amber, Paper, Monochrome)
## Three density presets (code::\micro::, code::\compact::, code::\extended::)
## Dual meter styles (code::\continuous:: and code::\led::)
## Peak-hold tracking with interactive click or keyboard ('r') reset
## Shared measurement broker: opening multiple meter windows never duplicates audio-server analysis synths
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates and displays a new SCVMeter window.

ARGUMENT:: server
The target link::Classes/Server:: (defaults to code::Server.default::).

ARGUMENT:: numIns
Number of input channels to meter.

ARGUMENT:: numOuts
Number of output channels to meter.

ARGUMENT:: theme
Theme name symbol (e.g. code::\graphite::, code::\phosphor::, code::\ice::, code::\amber::, code::\paper::, code::\monochrome::) or link::Classes/SCVTheme:: instance.

ARGUMENT:: density
Density preset: code::\micro::, code::\compact::, or code::\extended::.

ARGUMENT:: meterStyle
Meter display style: code::\continuous:: or code::\led::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: theme
Changes the active theme dynamically without restarting analysis synths.

METHOD:: density
Switches density mode and updates window dimensions.

METHOD:: meterStyle
Switches between continuous and segmented LED styling.

METHOD:: resetPeakHold
Resets peak-hold indicators to current levels.

METHOD:: close
Closes the meter window and unsubscribes from the broker.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;

// Default 2-in, 2-out compact meter in Graphite
m = SCVisuals.meter(s, 2, 2);

// Switch themes dynamically
m.theme = \ice;
m.theme = \phosphor;

// Switch density
m.density = \micro;
m.density = \compact;

// Close
m.close;
::
